                <pb facs="0648" n="578" sameAs="frus:frus1867p2/pg578"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">List of documents sent by the Mexican legation to the
                        Department of State of the United States, with the note of the 4th of
                        July,</hi> 1867, <hi rendition="#italic">in relation to the arrest of Don
                        Antonio Lopez de Santa Anna, at Sisal.</hi></head>
                <p>No. 1, June 21, .1867 ; the governor of Yucatan to Mr. Romero.</p>
                <p>No. 2, June 12, 1867; the same to the governor of Campeche.</p>
                <p>No. 3, June 15, 1867 ; the governor of Campeche to the governor of Yucatan.</p>
                <p>No. 4, June 15, 1867; Mr. Santa Anna to General Peraza.</p>
                <p>No. 5, June 15, 1867 ; Mr. Santa Anna to the citizens of Yucatan.</p>
                <p>No. 6, June 8, 1867.</p>
                <p>No. 7, June 8, 1867.</p>
                <p>No. 8, June 8, 1867; Mr. Vidaly Rivas to Don Antonio Taboada, commander of the
                    imperial garrison in Vera Cruz.</p>
                <p>No. 9, June 11, 1867 ; the same to a chief in Vera Cruz.</p>
                <p>No. 10, June 12; Mr. Santa Anna to General Peraza.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>IGNO. MARISCAL, <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary.</hi></signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-07-04"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 4, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>












